    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/212491": {
      "title": "Communications / Public Relations Specialist",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Communications / Public Relations Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Communications / Public Relations Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. We are only accepting applications submitted by October 12, 2026. Posting Details To navigate through this form, please use the “Prev” and “Save & Continue” buttons at the top of the page. Do not use your browser’s “Back” button as it will not save your progress and data will be lost. Posting Summary Logo Posting Number RTF00198PO26 USC Market Title Communications & Public Relations Specialist Link to USC Market Title https://uscjobs.sc.edu/titles/156210 Business Title (Internal Title) Communications / Public Relations Specialist Campus School of Medicine Columbia Work County Richland College/Division School of Medicine Columbia Department SOMC Communications Anticipated Hiring Range $53,576 $66,970 $80,364 Location of Vacancy Part/Full Time Full Time Hours per Week 40 Work Schedule Standard working schedule: 8:30am – 5:00pm Must be willing to work a flexible schedule to meet the needs of the department. Type of Staff Position Staff Time-Limited (STL) Basis 12 months Job Search Category Communication Services About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Benefits for Research Grant or Time-Limited Positions Are Indicated Below The University of South Carolina (UofSC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers employees a valuable benefits package, including health and life insurance, generous paid leave and retirement programs. To learn more about UofSC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Research Grant or Time-limited positions may be eligible for all, some, or no benefits, based on the grant or project funding. South Carolina Retirement Yes State Insurance Programs Yes Annual Leave Yes Sick Leave Yes Position Description Advertised Job Summary This position plays a critical coordination role across multiple communications functions, including USC Brain Health communications, the USC Floyd School of Medicine, university communications, and public information and communications teams within statewide partner organizations. This position supports USC Brain Health in advancing strategic communications, brand awareness, and public impact efforts across diverse audiences, including patients, the general public, legislators, and other key stakeholders. The role is responsible for developing and executing communications strategies that elevate the visibility, credibility, and influence of the USC Brain Health Network and USC Brain Health Center at the local, regional, and national levels. This position ensures alignment of messaging, consistency of brand voice, and effective dissemination of information across all platforms and collaborators. The role develops and manages content across owned and earned channels, strengthens relationships with internal and external partners, and supports media engagement to position USC Brain Health as the trusted leader in brain health. Job Related Minimum Required Education and Experience Requires a bachelor’s degree in a job related field and 2 or more years of job related experience, which may be substituted by an equivalent combination of job related certification, training, education, and/or experience. Required Certification, Licensure/Other Credentials Preferred Qualifications Strong understanding of strategic communications, public information, and storytelling across digital and traditional platforms Excellent writing and editing skills, including experience with AP Style Experience with media relations and event coordination Strong organizational and project management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities Experience coordinating communications across multiple organizations or stakeholder groups Demonstrates ability to translate complex health and research topics into clear, compelling content for varied audiences Familiarity with content management systems and analytics tools, and content design programs, such as Adobe Suite and Canva Ability to work effectively in a highly collaborative, fast-paced environment Experience with social media platforms Strong interpersonal skills and ability to build relationships with diverse stakeholders Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite Knowledge/Skills/Abilities Strong understanding of strategic communications, public information, and storytelling across digital and traditional platforms Excellent writing and editing skills, including experience with AP Style Experience with media relations and event coordination Strong organizational and project management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities Experience coordinating communications across multiple organizations or stakeholder groups Demonstrates ability to translate complex health and research topics into clear, compelling content for varied audiences Familiarity with content management systems and analytics tools, and content design programs, such as Adobe Suite and Canva Ability to work effectively in a highly collaborative, fast-paced environment Experience with social media platforms Strong interpersonal skills and ability to build relationships with diverse stakeholders Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite Required to conduct business lawfully and ethically by consistently adhering to compliance policies, procedures and regulations Job Duties Job Duty Strategic Communications Planning and Execution: In working with the Floyd School of Medicine director of strategic communications and Brain Health leadership, coordinate and implement integrated communications strategies and initiatives for USC Brain Health that increase awareness, strengthen public understanding, and highlight organizational impact. Coordinate messaging across multiple stakeholders, track outcomes, and provide regular updates to Floyd School of Medicine director of strategic communications and the Brain Health leadership team on communications effectiveness. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 35 Job Duty Public Relations, Stakeholder Engagement, and Coordination: Serve as a key liaison among USC Brain Health, USC Floyd School of Medicine, central USC communications, and external partner organizations. Build and maintain strong relationships with media, healthcare collaborators, and community organizations Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 30 Job Duty Writing and editing: Develop, write, and edit a wide range of communications materials, including press releases, brochures, newsletters, web content, social media copy, stakeholder updates, and thought leadership pieces. Ensure messaging is clear, accessible, accurate, engaging, and aligned with audience and organizational priorities. Maintain editorial calendars and ensure timely delivery of content. Collaborate with partners to ensure content is current, accurate, and consistent across platforms. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 30 Job Duty Other Duties: Perform other duties as assigned in support of the Floyd School of Medicine and Brain Health organizational missions and communications objectives. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 5 Position Attributes Hazardous weather category Non-Essential Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. No Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 09/16/2026 Position End Date 09/15/2027 Job Open Date 08/28/1926 Job Close Date 10/12/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. We are only accepting applications submitted by October 12, 2026. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/212489 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have at least a  Bachelor's Degree in a job related field and 2 or more years of job related experience, which may be substituted by an equivalent combination of job related certification, training, education, and/or experience? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume List of References and Contact Information Optional Documents Other Supporting Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
