    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/166328": {
      "title": "Student Landscape Technician",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Student Landscape Technician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Student Landscape Technician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number STU00031PO23 Job Title Student Employee Internal Title Student Landscape Technician Campus Upstate College/Division USC Upstate College/Division Level Department UPS Facilities Grounds & Housekeeping Advertised Salary $10.00 per hour Location of Vacancy USC Upstate, Spartanburg, SC Part/Full Time Part Time Hours per week 20 Work Schedule Generally works 10-15 hours per week (up to 20 hours max) between the hours of 6:30 a.m. to 3:30 p.m. Monday through Friday depending on class schedule. May have to work extended hours or weekend hours to support University activities. On occasion will assist the Building Maintenance crew and with setups. Exact work hours may be modified/variable to fit the season of the year. Can work up to 40 hours during summer break. Job Search Category Student Employee Position Description Advertised Job Summary Under supervision from the Director of Building & Landscape Services, is responsible for the preparation, management, and beautification of the campus. Perform the following functions on the campus: Prune and trim trees and shrubs Pick up and remove litter, leaves, and debris Weed both mechanically and chemically Plant, water, fertilize shrubs, flowers, trees, etc. Remove snow and ice from walks and roads Assist in maintenance of grounds equipment, tools, etc. In all functions, material that is mowed/pruned/cut/etc. is recycled (mulched, composted, etc.) Qualifications Must be a currently enrolled student at USC Upstate. Student must have a valid driver’s license with good driving record. Excellent communication and work ethic required. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1-2 Desired Start Date 04/01/2024 Job Open Date 04/01/2024 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/150138 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in educational or employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender (including transgender), gender identity or expression, genetic information, HIV /AIDs status, military status, national origin, pregnancy (false pregnancy, termination of pregnancy, childbirth, recovery therefrom or related medical conditions, breastfeeding), race, religion (including religious dress and grooming practices), sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other bases under federal, state, local law, or regulations. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your expected graduation date? (Open Ended Question) * What is your current cumulative GPA? (Open Ended Question) * Have you worked on-campus before? (Open Ended Question) * If yes, list department name and supervisor. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently working another on-campus job? (Open Ended Question) * If yes, list d