    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/209049": {
      "title": "Position Attributes",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Temporary Public Safety Officer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Temporary Public Safety Officer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is for the University of South Carolina Beaufort- Hilton Head Island Campus, Beaufort Campus, and Bluffton Campus. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number TMP01266PO26 Job Code Title Security Specialist III Advertised Title Temporary Public Safety Officer Campus Beaufort College/Division USC Beaufort College/Division Level Department BFT Public Safety Salary $25 hr. Location of Vacancy USCB campuses (BFT, BLUF, HHI) Part/Full Time Part Time Hours per Week 20 Work Schedule Hours will vary from week to week and weekend work will be expected (some evenings and holidays may be required). This posting is for as needed positions and no hours will be guaranteed. Job Search Category Law Enforcement About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Benefits for Temporary Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers temporary employees expected to work at least 30 hours per week health and life insurance, flexible spending accounts and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary USC Beaufort is seeking to hire a pool of qualified Temporary Public Safety Officers that will work on an as needed basis. Under the direction of the Director of Public Safety, these public safety officers provide security for all USC Beaufort campus locations(Beaufort, Bluffton, and Hilton Head Island) including but not limited to: providing a safe and secure environment for students, faculty, staff and campus visitors; preventing theft of and damage to equipment and contents of University buildings and property; deterring disorderly acts and unwanted intrusions at University buildings; all other duties as assigned, and enforcement of rules, regulations and policies as may be promulgated. Qualifications A high school education and one (1) year experience in law enforcement, military experience, safety or security activities preferred. A valid driver’s license and clean background check are required. Must have general computer skills, be able to communicate effectively, produce written reports, assess situations and develop a plan of action in a timely manner. Must be physically able to pursue an assailant, lift a person if necessary and act in emergency situations. Outdoor work required. First Responder training is desirable. Job Duties Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 10 Desired Start Date 07/30/2026 Proposed End Date 12/23/2026 Job Open Date 07/01/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant This position is for the University of South Carolina Beaufort- Hilton Head Island Campus, Beaufort Campus, and Bluffton Campus. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/208849 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in educational or employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender (including transgender), gender identity or expression, genetic information, HIV /AIDs status, military status, national origin, pregnancy (false pregnancy, termination of pregnancy, childbirth, recovery therefrom or related medical conditions, breastfeeding), race, religion (including religious dress and grooming practices), sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other bases under federal, state, local law, or regulations. Position Attributes Position Attributes Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. Safety/Security Sensitive or Requires a CDL Yes Hazardous weather category Essential Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This University of South Carolina Beaufort position is in Beaufort County South Carolina. Do you still wish to apply for this position? Yes No * Are you willing and able to submit to a pre-employment background check that may include, but it is not limited to, criminal history, national sex offender search and motor vehicle history as a condition of hire? Yes No * Do you have a valid Drivers License? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation 1 Resume List of References and Contact Information To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
