    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/212270": {
      "title": "Admissions & Financial Aid Assistant",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Admissions &amp; Financial Aid Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Admissions & Financial Aid Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. As part of the online process, a cover letter, resume, unofficial college transcripts and list of three references with contact information must be attached to the online application form. If you have any questions about the application procedures, please call (803) 938-3721. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number TMP02201PO26 Job Code Title Student Services Program Coordinator I Advertised Title Admissions & Financial Aid Assistant Campus Sumter College/Division USC Sumter College/Division Level Department USC Sumter - Palmetto College Salary 17.00 hour Location of Vacancy Part/Full Time Full Time Hours per Week 37.5 Work Schedule Job Search Category Student Services About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Benefits for Temporary Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers temporary employees expected to work at least 30 hours per week health and life insurance, flexible spending accounts and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary Position Summary The Admissions and Financial Aid Assistant works collaboratively with the Admissions and Financial Aid offices to provide support to new inquiries and scholarship recipients. In compliance with FERPA and Title IV requirements, the assistant uses the Student Information System (Banner), Salesforce CRM , and other communication tools to provide timely, professional outreach to prospective students and scholarship applicants. Primary Responsibilities · Utilize Salesforce CRM to review, manage, and document prospective student inquiries and communication activities. · Contact prospective students by telephone, email, and text messaging to provide information, answer general questions, and encourage continued engagement with the college. · Conduct timely follow-up with prospective students based on established recruitment and communication plans. · Accurately document all student contacts, responses, and outcomes in Salesforce. · Assist with reports by evaluating outreach efforts, tracking response and success rates, and identifying trends in student engagement. · Provide general support to the Admissions Office and assist with recruitment activities, campus events, and other college-sponsored programs as needed. · Perform other related duties that support the recruitment and enrollment goals of the college. · Provide general support to the Financial Aid Office by managing front desk operations. · Assist the Office of Financial Aid in compiling information from scholarship applications and new student information from CRM . · Maintain accurate and organized records of scholarship recipients, award amounts, and renewal status based on decisions made by the scholarship committee. · Verify student enrollment of scholarship recipients for relevant terms and track the submission of required scholarship documents of scholarship recipients. · Respond to inquiries about scholarship opportunities, requirements, and application status. · Work closely with the Office of Financial Aid and the scholarship committee. · Prepare summary reports for the Office of Financial Aid, scholarship committee, and the Development Coordinator. · Attend scholarship committee meetings as needed. Minimum Qualifications · Requires a bachelor’s degree in a job-related field and no prior work experience. · Excellent written and verbal communication skills. · Strong computer skills and the ability to learn and effectively use Salesforce CRM and other technology platforms. · Ability to work independently, manage multiple responsibilities, and follow established procedures. · Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. · Ability to communicate professionally and effectively with students, prospective students, and families. · Dependable, self-motivated, and comfortable working in a fast-paced, student-centered environment. · Ability to maintain confidentiality and appropriately handle student information. Preferred Qualifications · Previous experience in college admissions, recruitment, customer service, sales, call center operations, record-keeping, or related field. · Experience using Salesforce or another customer relationship management ( CRM ) system. · Experience using a Student Information System, such as Banner. · Experience using Microsoft Office Suite programs, especially Excel and Outlook. · Familiarity with higher education enrollment, recruitment processes, and the maintenance of financial aid records. Work Schedule Full-time weekly work schedule focused primarily on CRM operations, the management of leads and inquiries, and maintaining and tracking accurate scholarship information. Qualifications Requires a bachelor’s degree in a job-related field and no prior work experience. Job Duties Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date 09/01/2026 Proposed End Date Job Open Date 08/25/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant As part of the online process, a cover letter, resume, unofficial college transcripts and list of three references with contact information must be attached to the online application form. If you have any questions about the application procedures, please call (803) 938-3721. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/212260 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Position Attributes Position Attributes Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. Safety/Security Sensitive or Requires a CDL No Hazardous weather category Non-Essential Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Other Supporting Documents Resume List of References and Contact Information Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/211597": {
      "title": "Communication Graphic Designer",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Communication Graphic Designer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Communication Graphic Designer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. We are only accepting applications submitted by September 23, 2026. This posting is a re-advertisement. Applications previously submitted are all being considered. Previous applicants do not need to reapply. Posting Details To navigate through this form, please use the “Prev” and “Save & Continue” buttons at the top of the page. Do not use your browser’s “Back” button as it will not save your progress and data will be lost. Posting Summary Logo Posting Number RTF00151PO26 USC Market Title Communications Coordinator Link to USC Market Title https://uscjobs.sc.edu/titles/166610 Business Title Communication Graphic Designer Campus Columbia Work County Richland College/Division College of Education Department CED College of Education Location of Vacancy This is a hybrid position. Part/Full Time Full Time Hours per Week 37.5 Type of Faculty Position Staff Time-Limited (STL) Basis 12 months Job Search Category Communication Services About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Benefits for Research Grant or Time-Limited Positions Are Indicated Below The University of South Carolina (UofSC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers employees a valuable benefits package, including health and life insurance, generous paid leave and retirement programs. To learn more about UofSC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Research Grant or Time-limited positions may be eligible for all, some, or no benefits, based on the grant or project funding. South Carolina Retirement Yes State Insurance Programs Yes Annual Leave Yes Sick Leave Yes Position Description Advertised Job Summary The Communications Graphic Designer will work as part of the team responsible for SC TEACHER’s communications brand and the expansion and implementation of communications strategies and policies to support the strategic goals of SC TEACHER . As part of the communications team, this position will have responsibilities spanning research report design; creation of graphics for social media, marketing, and team presentations; and event preparation and setup, along with other opportunities to support overall communications and operations. Job Related Minimum Required Education and Experience Requires a bachelor’s degree in a job related field and 2 or more years of job related experience, which may be substituted by an equivalent combination of job related certification, training, education, and/or experience. Required Certification, Licensure/Other Credentials Preferred Qualifications Strong skills with Adobe Creative Cloud, particularly Illustrator and InDesign Ability to apply visual design principles and specific brand guidelines to any project Strong visual communication skills, including presentation creation and brand adherence Experience with project management and/or event coordination Knowledge/Skills/Abilities Demonstrated experience with Adobe illustrator and inDesign Attention to detail and organizational skills. Familiarity with web design and HTML Ability to proofread and follow a style guide Experience with a project management system (e.g., Monday, Asana, Basecamp) Job Duties Job Duty Graphic Design: Execute and coordinate graphic design of research materials such as monthly reports and data visualization. Collaborate with members of communications and research teams to take ideas from early draft to full design, both print and online, using design principles and brand adherence. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 40 Job Duty Marketing Materials Creation: To further encourage stakeholder engagement with research and events, design and support creation of marketing materials such as postcards, handouts, flyers, and event materials, in accordance with the SC TEACHER brand and team goals. Support brand development through graphic design and visual assets. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 30 Job Duty Event Preparation and Coordination: Collaborate with event facilitators, operations team, and communications team to prep necessary materials for SC TEACHER events, such as swag, handouts, branded décor, and items for facilitation. Work across teams to establish, gather, and transport materials for successful event execution. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 20 Job Duty Project Management: Contribute to the team’s overall organization and efficiency by tracking project goals and steps to achieve those goals, as well as relevant discussions and important information, in project management system (Basecamp). Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 10 Position Attributes Hazardous weather category Non-Essential Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. No Posting Detail Information Desired Start Date 08/01/2026 Position End Date Job Open Date 06/25/2026 Job Close Date 09/23/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. We are only accepting applications submitted by September 23, 2026. This posting is a re-advertisement. Applications previously submitted are all being considered. Previous applicants do not need to reapply. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/208328 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in educational or employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender (including transgender), gender identity or expression, genetic information, HIV /AIDs status, military status, national origin, pregnancy (false pregnancy, termination of pregnancy, childbirth, recovery therefrom or related medical conditions, breastfeeding), race, religion (including religious dress and grooming practices), sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other bases under federal, state, local law, or regulations. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have at least a bachelor's degree in a job related field and 2 or more years of job related experience, which may be substituted by an equivalent combination of job related certification, training, education, and/or experience? Yes No * Do you have graphic design experience? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume List of References and Contact Information Optional Documents Other Supporting Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
