 place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Benefits for Temporary Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers temporary employees expected to work at least 30 hours per week health and life insurance, flexible spending accounts and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary Painter Do you enjoy not sitting behind a desk? Do you enjoy helping USC Students? Do you enjoy troubleshooting challenges by finding solutions, especially unique challenges? This is the job for you. Will assist supervisor with selection, preparation and application of paint and other decorative finishes to various types of surfaces in the residence halls, including plaster, wood, sheet rock metal, etc. Under general and direct supervision, will perform these activities in conformance with Federal, state, city and county codes and standards and within any current and future guidelines developed and to be developed by USC and the Department of Housing. Performs necessary surface preparation to surfaces such as stripping, sanding, and reparing as necessary prior to application of paint and decorative finishes. This position has been designated as essential personnel during inclement/ hazardous weather and other emergencies. Essential Job Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Apply decorative coating to multiple surfaces following procedures 2. Follow work management procedures 3. Prepares and applies patching, plaster, caulking and other compounds as needed This position is designated as essential personnel during inclement/hazardous weather and other emergencies. Potential for Full Time Employee ( FTE ) position based on job performance. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency. Valid Driver’s License required. Job Duties Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies multiple Desired Start Date 07/16/2026 Proposed End Date 12/18/2026 Job Open Date 07/08/2026 Job Close Date 10/31/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant Please include all relevant experience, to include any jobs with USC on the application. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/209166 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Position Attributes Position Attributes Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. Safety/Security Sensitive or Requires a CDL No Hazardous weather category Essential Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have at least a High School Diploma/or equivalent (GED)? Yes No * Do you have a Valid Driver's License? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume List of References and Contact Information To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
