    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/206501": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. If you have any questions about the position or the application process, please contact Dr. Tessa Hastings, Search Committee Chair, at hastint@mailbox.sc.edu. Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number FAC00020PO25 Advertised Title Assistant Professor Campus Columbia College/Division College of Pharmacy Department COP Clinical Pharmacy and Outcomes Sciences Advertised Salary Range Commensurate with qualifications Location of Vacancy Part/Full Time Full Time Hours per Week 37.5 Position Category Full-time Equivalent (FTE) Basis 12 months Work County Richland Tenure Information Tenure-Track/Tenured Job Search Category Faculty About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Veterans' Preference Statement The University of South Carolina is committed to equal opportunity and proudly values the skills and experience military veterans bring to our workforce. Across South Carolina, we are making veterans a priority for employment and recognize their vital contributions to our state and our communities. Benefits for FTE Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers state employees a valuable benefits package, including health and life insurance, generous paid leave and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary The University of South Carolina College of Pharmacy ( USC COP ) invites applications for one full-time 12-month tenure-track faculty position at the level of Assistant Professor in the Department of Clinical Pharmacy and Outcomes Sciences ( CPOS ) with a focus on community pharmacy practice. We seek an innovative pharmacist who will build and sustain innovative services that advance patient care and expand access to high-quality pharmacy services, with an appreciation for the evolving roles of regulatory affairs and emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence, in healthcare delivery. This position is embedded within a well-established independent community pharmacy group with multiple locations across South Carolina, offering a diverse range of services including traditional dispensing, sterile and non-sterile compounding, durable medical equipment, and enhanced patient care services. The successful candidate will play a key role in developing and maintaining community pharmacy-based services. This will serve as a platform for patient care, trainee learning, and practice innovation. Responsibilities will include contributing to the teaching mission of the College, engaging in service activities, and participating in scholarly work in collaboration with departmental faculty to support existing research and grant-funded initiatives, while also contributing to the development of new collaborative research programs and externally funded opportunities. Scholarly activities may include practice-based research, quality improvement initiatives, evaluation of patient care services, or other areas such as implementation science, with opportunities to explore the application of regulatory science, data-driven approaches, and artificial intelligence to advance pharmacy practice. Applicants are expected to contribute to USC’s vision of transforming pharmacy practice through patient-centered services that improve outcomes and increase access to care, while recognizing the importance of regulatory frameworks and innovative technologies in shaping the future of healthcare. The ideal candidate will be collaborative, committed to excellence in teaching and practice, and interested in developing forward-thinking approaches to community pharmacy care. Candidates are expected to contribute to and uphold the USC College of Pharmacy’s culture of collaboration, innovation, and patient-centered impact (https://sc.edu/study/colleges_schools/pharmacy/about/vision_mission/). Located in the heart of South Carolina, USC offers an exceptional quality of life, with affordable housing, thriving arts and culture, and proximity to beautiful outdoor spaces. Additionally, USC is a family-friendly institution with resources to support life-work balance, including on-campus childcare and dual-career services. The University of South Carolina is committed to fostering an inclusive academic environment that is open, welcoming, and supportive of individuals of all backgrounds. The COP actively promotes equity and access to ensure all faculty, staff, and students thrive. We celebrate the diverse voices, perspectives, and experiences of our employees. Required Education and Experience Qualified candidates must possess a PharmD, PhD, MD or equivalent terminal degree. Applicants should have a strong background in regulatory or quality science with experience in biopharmaceuticals, medical devices, or regulatory agencies. Candidates should have excellent written and verbal communication skills. Preferred Qualifications N/A Posting Detail Information Desired Start Date 08/16/2026 Job Open Date 02/11/2025 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant If you have any questions about the position or the application process, please contact Dr. Tessa Hastings, Search Committee Chair, at hastint@mailbox.sc.edu. Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/183305 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in educational or employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender (including transgender), gender identity or expression, genetic information, HIV /AIDs status, military status, national origin, pregnancy (false pregnancy, termination of pregnancy, childbirth, recovery therefrom or related medical conditions, breastfeeding), race, religion (including religious dress and grooming practices), sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other bases under federal, state, local law, or regulations. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References and Contact Information Teaching Statement Research Statement Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/211214": {
      "title": "Envir Svs Specialist/ Part Time",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Envir Svs Specialist/ Part Time Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Envir Svs Specialist/ Part Time Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number TMP01939PO26 Job Code Title Building/Grounds Specialist II Advertised Title Envir Svs Specialist/ Part Time Campus Beaufort College/Division USC Beaufort College/Division Level Department BFT Facilities Planning Salary $17.00 Location of Vacancy USC Beaufort supported area Part/Full Time Part Time Hours per Week 25 Work Schedule Schedule will be determined by the supervisor. Must be available nights and weekends. Job Search Category Other Professional About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Benefits for Temporary Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers temporary employees expected to work at least 30 hours per week health and life insurance, flexible spending accounts and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary Help Create a Clean, Safe, and Welcoming Campus for Every Student The University of South Carolina Beaufort ( USCB ) is seeking two energetic, dependable, and service-oriented Part-Time Environmental Services Specialists to join our Facilities team. If you take pride in creating clean, healthy, and welcoming environments while making a meaningful impact every day, we invite you to become part of one of South Carolina’s fastest-growing universities. Located in the heart of the breathtaking South Carolina Lowcountry, USCB offers a unique opportunity to work in a vibrant academic community surrounded by coastal beauty, historic charm, and an exceptional quality of life. Every classroom, office, residence hall, and gathering space you help maintain contributes directly to the success of our students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Why Join USCB ? At USCB , every employee plays an important role in creating an exceptional campus experience. As an Environmental Services Specialist, you will help ensure our facilities remain clean, safe, and ready to support learning, research, athletics, and community engagement. What You’ll Do As a member of the Facilities team, you will: Perform routine custodial and environmental services in assigned campus buildings. Clean, sanitize, and maintain classrooms, offices, restrooms, laboratories, common areas, and other university facilities. Maintain floors through sweeping, mopping, vacuuming, and other approved cleaning methods. Empty trash and recycling containers and replenish custodial supplies. Assist with campus event setup and breakdown, including tables, chairs, and meeting spaces. Safely operate custodial equipment and use cleaning chemicals in accordance with university safety procedures. Follow health and safety practices related to Bloodborne Pathogens and workplace sanitation. Help maintain an attractive, welcoming environment for students, faculty, staff, visitors, and community partners. Perform other related custodial and maintenance duties as assigned. What We’re Looking For Successful candidates will demonstrate: Knowledge of custodial cleaning methods and equipment. Ability to safely read, understand, and follow cleaning product labels and safety warnings. Strong work ethic with attention to detail. Dependability, professionalism, and excellent customer service. Ability to work independently and as part of a collaborative team. Physical ability to perform custodial duties, including standing, walking, lifting, bending, pushing, and carrying equipment and supplies throughout the workday. Commitment to maintaining a safe, clean, and welcoming campus environment. Why You’ll Love Working at USCB Flexible part-time schedule Supportive and team-oriented work environment Beautiful coastal campus locations in Beaufort and Bluffton Opportunity to serve students and the university community every day Meaningful work that helps create an exceptional college experience Be Part of Something Bigger Every clean classroom, every prepared event space, and every welcoming campus begins with a dedicated Environmental Services team. Join the University of South Carolina Beaufort and help create spaces where students learn, faculty teach, and our community thrives. Apply today and help keep USCB looking its very best! Please be prepared to upload a current resume. Qualifications Typically holds a high school diploma or GED . Requires 1 or more years of job related experience. Job Duties Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 2 Desired Start Date 08/12/2026 Proposed End Date Job Open Date 08/07/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/211209 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in educational or employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender (including transgender), gender identity or expression, genetic information, HIV /AIDs status, military status, national origin, pregnancy (false pregnancy, termination of pregnancy, childbirth, recovery therefrom or related medical conditions, breastfeeding), race, religion (including religious dress and grooming practices), sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other bases under federal, state, local law, or regulations. Position Attributes Position Attributes Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. Safety/Security Sensitive or Requires a CDL No Hazardous weather category Non-Essential Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Other Supporting Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
