kills/Abilities Written and verbal communication skills. Ability to prioritize and be flexible. Proficient in the use of Microsoft Office. Job Duties Job Duty Coordinates all scheduling and referral processes for Brain Health Network patients and providers, including, but not limited to, scheduling patient appointments, conducting patient reminder calls, authorizing services, handling medical records, following up with patients and providers, and creating/maintaining schedule templates. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 40 Job Duty Assists with data input and data management functions related to patient care and research activities for the Brain Health Network. Ensures data is entered within 24 hours of rendered services and provides reports to providers within 24 hours of receipt of completed reports/summaries. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 30 Job Duty Serves as primary point of contact for Brain Health Network patient operations. Responds within 24 hours to all phone and email messages and helps ensures timely and continuous communication between Brain Health team members and across all Brain Health Network sites. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 20 Job Duty Performs other duties as requested or as assigned. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 10 Position Attributes Hazardous weather category Non-Essential Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. No Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date Position End Date Job Open Date 09/03/2026 Job Close Date 10/18/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. 