      "title": "Position Attributes",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Bus Driver Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Bus Driver Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please ensure that you include all work experience in your application, along with detailed descriptions of your job duties and responsibilities for each position. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number TMP02240PO26 Job Code Title Administrative Specialist I Advertised Title Bus Driver Campus Columbia College/Division Division of Administration and Finance Department DAF Parking and Transportation Services Salary $20-$25/hr based on shift Location of Vacancy Part/Full Time Part Time Hours per Week 35 Work Schedule There is potential for additional hours depending on the needs of the department. Hours vary. Must be willing to work a flexible schedule to meet the needs of the department. Work schedule may include weekends and nights. Job Search Category Transportation/Parking About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Benefits for Temporary Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers temporary employees expected to work at least 30 hours per week health and life insurance, flexible spending accounts and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary CDL Required University of South Carolina Shuttle Drivers transport students, faculty and staff throughout the Columbia Campus daily. Shuttle Drivers are also responsible for reporting maintenance concerns promptly, keep rider log and a clean environment for riders. Drivers are on duty days, nights, weekends, and some holidays. Must have Class A with P endorsements and V restrictions or Class B with P endorsements, DOT Card and 6 months CDL driving experience. Qualifications Must have 6 months bus driver experience. Have a good driving record. Requirements of class A with P endorsements and V restrictions or Class B with P endorsements, DOT Card and 6 months CDL driving experience. Job Duties Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 10 Desired Start Date 09/01/2026 Proposed End Date Job Open Date 09/01/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Please ensure that you include all work experience in your application, along with detailed descriptions of your job duties and responsibilities for each position. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/212618 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Position Attributes Position Attributes Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. Safety/Security Sensitive or Requires a CDL Yes Hazardous weather category Essential Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a valid Commercial Driver’s License (CDL)? Yes No * Do you have a Class A with P endorsements and V restrictions or Class B with P endorsements and DOT card? Yes No * Do you have 6 months bus driver experience? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume List of References and Contact Information Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
