    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/212413": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Facilities Operations",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Assistant Director of Facilities Operations - Health Science Campus Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Assistant Director of Facilities Operations - Health Science Campus Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. We are only accepting applications submitted by October 9, 2026. The University of South Carolina offers a valuable benefits package including but not limited to: Health and Life Insurance Retirement Programs Paid Tuition Dependent Scholarships Annual Leave Sick Leave 13 Paid Holidays (including an extended December holiday) Paid Parental Leave Professional Development Opportunities Click here to learn more about why you should work at USC. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number STA00651PO26 Job Family Building and Grounds Maintenance Job Function Facilities Management USC Market Title Asst. Director of Maintenance Link to USC Market Title https://uscjobs.sc.edu/titles/187720 Job Level M3 - Managerial Business Title (Internal Title) Assistant Director of Facilities Operations - Health Science Campus Campus Columbia Work County Richland College/Division Division of Administration and Finance Department DAF Facilities Maintenance State Pay Range G11 USC Market Range MRJ - $78,441 $98,051 $117,662 Anticipated Hiring Range $78,441- $98,051 Location of Vacancy Part/Full Time Full Time Hours per Week 37.5 Work Schedule Monday-Friday 8:00a.m-4:30p.m. Must be willing to work a flexible schedule to accommodate the needs of the department. Basis 12 months Job Search Category Trades/Maintenance About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Veterans' Preference Statement The University of South Carolina is committed to equal opportunity and proudly values the skills and experience military veterans bring to our workforce. Across South Carolina, we are making veterans a priority for employment and recognize their vital contributions to our state and our communities. Benefits for FTE Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers employees a valuable benefits package, including health and life insurance, generous paid leave and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Research Grant or Time-limited positions may be eligible for all, some, or no benefits, based on the grant or project funding. Position Description Advertised Job Summary Under limited supervision, provides leadership, planning, coordination, budget management, and operational oversight for maintenance and operations at the University of South Carolina Health Science Campus ( HSC ). The position reports to the Director of Services and manages Health Science Campus maintenance operations, maintenance planning, preventive and corrective maintenance coordination, AiM CMMS utilization, work order accountability, inspections, customer service, and reporting. The position supervises the comprehensive campus maintenance operations team consisting of a Quality Control Manager, Maintenance Supervisor, Crew Lead, two Maintenance Technicians, and an HVAC /Controls Technician. This position serves as the primary facilities operations liaison for the Health Science Campus and coordinates with building occupants in all HSC buildings, Facilities leadership, project managers, contractors, vendors, custodial contractors, in-house landscape staff, Environmental Health and Safety, and other University departments. The position manages the annual budget for maintenance operations, capital renewal/refurbishments, capital replacements, and ensures labor hours, material costs, building-related costs, and all expenditures are tracked through AiM and supporting fiscal processes. The position is responsible for both the campus and building-level maintenance operations and coordination for systems including HVAC , controls, electrical, plumbing, life safety, emergency generator systems, automatic transfer switches, emergency power panels, high-voltage service coordination, building envelope, site conditions, and related infrastructure. The position coordinates closely with the Central Utility Plant team regarding chilled water to the Health Science Campus, including planned outages, unplanned interruptions, issue escalation, occupant communication, and service restoration updates. Job Related Minimum Required Education and Experience Requires a bachelor’s degree in a job related field and 5 or more years of job related experience, which may be substituted by an equivalent combination of certification, training, education and/or experience. Required Certification, Licensure/Other Credentials Valid driver’s license required. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in facilities management, engineering, construction management, business/public administration, or a related field and 8 or more years of progressively responsible experience in facilities maintenance operations, maintenance planning, building systems coordination, or construction turnover. Experience in academic, research, healthcare-adjacent, laboratory, or high-visibility institutional facilities preferred. Experience supervising maintenance personnel, using AiM or a similar CMMS , managing budgets, coordinating capital renewal/refurbishment and replacement planning, overseeing custodial contractor quality, and coordinating landscape inspections/projects is preferred. Certified Educational Facilities Manager ( CEFP ) or Certified Facilities Manager ( CFM ) are also highly desirable. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities Extensive understanding of preventive and corrective maintenance programs for complex institutional facilities, including HVAC , controls, plumbing, electrical, life safety, emergency power, building automation, and general building systems. Proficiency with AiM or similar CMMS platforms, including work order management, PM compliance, labor and material cost tracking, budget reporting, and maintenance performance reporting. Experience training staff in CMMS utilization and ensuring accountability for timely and accurate documentation of labor hours, materials, costs, expenditures, and work completion. Skilled in managing annual maintenance budgets and supporting capital renewal, refurbishment, and replacement planning. Experience coordinating with CUP personnel regarding chilled water and steam outages affecting assigned buildings, while recognizing that CUP operations and maintenance are not direct responsibilities of this position. Familiarity with emergency generators, automatic transfer switches, emergency power distribution, and high-voltage electrical coordination; high-voltage switching, testing, and maintenance must be performed by properly qualified personnel or contractors. Strong leadership, communication, customer service, inspection, reporting, problem-solving, and team-building skills. Understanding of safety practices, codes, regulations, lockout/tagout principles, PPE , and safe work practices in active facilities environments. Skilled in coordinating preparation, response, communication, inspection, and recovery activities for hazardous weather and campus continuity events affecting the Health Science Campus, including storms, inclement weather, ice/snow, severe thunderstorms, tropical weather, flooding/water intrusion, and debris issues. Job Duties Job Duty Responsible for managing Health Science Campus maintenance operations, preventive maintenance, corrective maintenance, maintenance planning, and work management. Establishes, reviews, and maintains planned and corrective maintenance schedules for assigned buildings and systems including HVAC , controls, electrical, plumbing, life safety, emergency power, building envelope, exterior/site-related conditions, and general building systems. Plans, inspects, verifies, communicates, and troubleshoots facility maintenance issues; assigns and prioritizes work orders; monitors backlog and recurring issues; ensures corrective measures are completed; and ensures all work is planned, delivered, documented, and completed safely, effectively, and in accordance with University standards, departmental procedures, and applicable codes and regulations. Ensures AiM is utilized as the CMMS for work orders, preventive maintenance, labor tracking, material usage, material costs, building-related expenditures, and maintenance reporting. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 30 Job Duty Responsible for supervising, directing, training, hiring, performance reviews, and holding accountable the Health Science Campus comprehensive maintenance and operations staff consisting of a Quality Control Manager, Maintenance Supervisor, Crew Lead, two Maintenance Technicians, and an HVAC /Controls Technician. Assigns work based on employee capabilities, job classifications, service priorities, safety requirements, and building operational needs; reviews work assignments and performance; monitors labor hours and materials expended; provides direction, leadership, motivation, and on-the-job training; ensures accurate documentation of labor hours and materials in AiM; and promotes safe, productive, customer-focused, and cost-effective service delivery. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 15 Job Duty Responsible for coordinating building systems, utility service impacts, emergency power, and high-voltage-related service coordination for assigned facilities. Coordinates with qualified personnel, vendors, contractors, utility representatives, and Facilities leadership regarding emergency generator systems, automatic transfer switches, emergency power panels, electrical distribution, high-voltage infrastructure, switchgear/transformer concerns, outage planning, and required testing or maintenance. Coordinates closely with Central Utility Plant personnel regarding chilled water and steam service to the Health Science Campus, including planned outages, unplanned interruptions, issue escalation, occupant communication, and service restoration updates. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 15 Job Duty Responsible for custodial contractor oversight, landscape inspections, and quality control coordination. Oversees service quality for outsourced custodial services by coordinating inspections, reviewing contractor performance, documenting deficiencies, communicating service expectations, and following up on corrective actions. Coordinates with the Quality Control Manager for on-site inspections and reporting related to maintenance planning, custodial inspections, and landscape inspections. Coordinates inspections of landscape conditions, exterior appearance, hardscape conditions, irrigation concerns, plant health, litter, drainage concerns, and site issues maintained by in-house landscape staff. Provides coordination for landscaping projects, landscape maintenance initiatives, seasonal improvements, service enhancements, and corrective actions affecting the Health Science Campus. Coordinates inspections and follow-up actions for landscape project impacts, landscape maintenance initiatives, storm preparation, post-storm exterior inspections, debris concerns, hardscape/sidewalk impacts, and weather-related custodial or site appearance needs. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 10 Job Duty Serves as the primary facilities operations liaison for the Health Science Campus. Communicates regularly with the Director of Services, building occupants, researchers, faculty, staff, students, Facilities leadership, contractors, vendors, custodial contractors, in-house landscape staff, project managers, EHS , IT, security/access control, Parking and Transportation as applicable, and other support departments. Provides prompt customer service, research issues, communicates status updates, gathers necessary information, gives maintenance guidance, coordinates service impacts, and escalates matters requiring leadership direction. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 10 Job Duty Responsible for managing and reporting on the annual budget for Health Science Campus maintenance operations, capital renewal/refurbishments, and capital replacements. Monitors and tracks expenditures, labor hours, material costs, service contract costs, repair costs, capital renewal/refurbishment needs, capital replacement needs, and other building-related costs. Uses AiM data and supporting financial information to prepare reports, identify cost trends, support budget forecasts, document unfunded needs, recommend priorities, and provide the Director of Services with accurate planning and decision-making information. Coordinates with business, accounting, procurement, project management, and Facilities leadership personnel to ensure resources are used effectively and expenditures are properly documented. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 10 Job Duty Supports construction turnover, commissioning, warranty tracking, and operational readiness for new or modified Health Science Campus facilities and systems. Participates in turnover walks, commissioning coordination, training coordination, punch list review, deficiency tracking, and operational readiness planning. Coordinates with project teams, commissioning agents, contractors, vendors, and Facilities stakeholders to support receipt and review of asset lists, O&M manuals, staff training documentation, warranties, spare parts/attic stock, as-builts, BAS sequences, emergency power documentation, high-voltage coordination points, and PM recommendations. Supports AiM setup and validates asset information, maintenance locations, PM requirements, warranty flags, and work order routing needs. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 5 Job Duty Responds to emergency maintenance situations as needed during and after normal business hours, including serving in an on-call capacity as needed, by communicating with Facilities personnel, the Director of Services, maintenance staff, USC Police Department dispatch, CUP personnel, contractors, utility representatives, or governing municipality representatives as appropriate. Coordinates response and communication for utility outages, chilled water or steam service interruptions, generator/emergency power events, HVAC failures, electrical issues, leaks, hazardous weather events, storms, inclement weather, ice/snow events, severe thunderstorms, tropical weather impacts, flooding/water intrusion, debris issues, life safety concerns, and other building operations emergencies. Coordinates pre-event readiness checks, site inspections, occupant communication, staffing coordination, post-event damage assessments, and follow-up maintenance actions as appropriate. Ensures leadership is notified when a utility or critical system is shut down or when an outage, weather event, or facility condition may affect occupants, research operations, academic activities, safety, or campus continuity. Performs other duties as assigned. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 5 Position Attributes Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. Safety Sensitive or Security Sensitive Yes Hazardous weather category Essential Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date Job Open Date 08/27/2026 Job Close Date 10/09/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. We are only accepting applications submitted by October 9, 2026. The University of South Carolina offers a valuable benefits package including but not limited to: Health and Life Insurance Retirement Programs Paid Tuition Dependent Scholarships Annual Leave Sick Leave 13 Paid Holidays (including an extended December holiday) Paid Parental Leave Professional Development Opportunities Click here to learn more about why you should work at USC . Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/212285 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have at least a Bachelor’s degree in a job related field and 5 or more years of job related experience, which may be substituted by an equivalent combination of job related certification, training, education, and/or experience? Yes No * Do you have a valid driver's license? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume List of References and Contact Information Optional Documents Cover Letter To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
