      "title": "Personal Trainer",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Personal Trainer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Personal Trainer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number STU00005PO24 Job Title Student Employee Internal Title Personal Trainer Campus Upstate College/Division USC Upstate College/Division Level Department UPS Campus Recreation Advertised Salary $14 per hour depending on certifications Location of Vacancy USC Upstate, Spartanburg, SC Part/Full Time Part Time Hours per week 10 Work Schedule Up to 10 hours per week. Weekly scheduled to be determined and will vary, but student employee must be able to work flexible hours to include some evenings and weekends Job Search Category Student Employee Position Description Advertised Job Summary Provide safe and effective workout routines for Wellness Center clients. Enforce all policies of the Wellness Center: ensure clients conduct themselves in an orderly manner. Report all problems to the Facility Supervisor Personal Trainers are responsible for providing customer service and enforcement of the facilities policies and procedures. Personal Trainers will also be responsible for performing Fitness Assessments, New Member Facility Orientations, and Program Developments for clients. Typical Responsibilities Performing Fitness Assessments to all prospective clients and on request of client Meet with clients and perform quality program developments for customers as needed Assist in the enforcement of Wellness Center policy and procedures specifically in the Weight Room and Fitness Center Assist in handling all emergency situations as needed Assisting with all areas of promotions of the Personal Training program (may include programs and sessions outside of the Wellness Center) Intervene in disputes and actions of unsafe behavior Report all accidents and incidents to supervisor Assist in educating all users of the Weight Room and Wellness Center safe techniques and proper lifting form (or as requested by patrons) Daily checks of equipment to ensure proper function and safety Other duties as assigned by supervisor Qualifications Satisfactory completion of staff training provided by the Wellness Center Staff Must be able to work well as a team player and independently. Must demonstrate quality customer service skills. Must obtain CPR / AED certification within one month of employment. Must obtain a current National Fitness Certification (i.e.: ACE , AFAA , NETA , ACSM , etc.) within 3 months of employment Preferred Qualifications Exercise Science Major Excellent problem solving and critical thinking ability Preference given to students who have previous work experience or course work in Health and Human Performance or Exercise Science and previous experience in personal training. Preference given to work-study Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 2-5 Desired Start Date 01/22/2024 Job Open Date 12/01/2023 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/162890 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in educational or employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender (including transgender), gender identity or expression, genetic information, HIV /AIDs status, military status, national origin, pregnancy (false pregnancy, termination of pregnancy, childbirth, recovery therefrom or related medical conditions, breastfeeding), race, religion (including religious dress and grooming practices), sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other bases under federal, state, local law, or regulations. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your expected graduation date? (Open Ended Question) * What is your current cumulative GPA? (Open Ended Question) * Have you worked on-campus before? (Open Ended Question) * If yes, list department name and supervisor. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently working another on-campus job? (Open Ended Question) * If yes, list department name and supervisor. (Open Ended Question) * Have you been awarded Federal Work Study for this semester? Yes No * What is your major? (Open Ended Question) * What is your current student status? Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student * What is your College affiliation? Please list one of the following: Business Administration & Economics College of Arts & Sciences Department of Psychology Education Fine Arts & Communication Studies Interdisciplinary Studies Information Management Systems Language, Literature & Composition Math & Computer Science Natural Sciences Non-Profit Administration Nursing Pre-Professional Social & Behavioral Sciences Social Sciences, Philosophy & History Undeclared (Open Ended Question) * Why are you interested in this position? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a current National Fitness Certification (i.e.: ACE, AFAA, NETA, ACSM, etc.)? If selected for interview, be prepared to show proof. Yes No * If yes, when does your National Fitness Certification expire? If selected for an interview, be prepared to show proof. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter Resume List of References and Contact Information To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
