e of Human Resources, USC Union, PO Drawer 729, Union, SC 29379. If you have any questions about the application procedures, please call 864-424-8027. If you are hired to teach for USC Union, you will be required to submit an official copy of your graduate transcripts. Review of credentials will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/129455 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in educational or employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender (including transgender), gender identity or expression, genetic information, HIV /AIDs status, military status, national origin, pregnancy (false pregnancy, termination of pregnancy, childbirth, recovery therefrom or related medical conditions, breastfeeding), race, religion (including religious dress and grooming practices), sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other bases under federal, state, local law, or regulations. Position Attributes Position Attributes Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. Safety/Security Sensitive or Requires a CDL No Hazardous weather category Non-Essential Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you willing and able to submit to a pre-employment background check that may include, but it is not limited to, criminal history, national sex offender search and motor vehicle history as a condition of hire? Yes No * Do you have a Master's degree with 18 graduate credit hours in the teaching discipline that you desire to be approved? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Other Supporting Documents Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/191632": {
      "title": "Position Attributes",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Part-time Evning Housekper Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Part-time Evning Housekper Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number TMP00727PO25 Job Code Title Building/Grounds Specialist II Advertised Title Part-time Evning Housekper Campus Columbia College/Division Division of Student Affairs and Academic Support Department SAAS UHS Health Services Salary $17.00 per hour Location of Vacancy Part/Full Time Part Time Hours per Week 30 Work Schedule 4pm-10pm Mon-Friday Must be willing to work a flexible schedule to meet the needs of the department. Job Search Category Trades/Maintenance About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Benefits for Temporary Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers temporary employees expected to work at least 30 hours per week health and life insurance, flexible spending accounts and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary The Evening Housekeeper position is responsible for all areas of operation including, but not limited to, regular cleaning of the Center for Health and Well-Being and Thomson Building, reporting of facility issues, assisting with recycling efforts, maintaining minimal stock levels of custodial supplies. Compensation for the Housekeeper starts at $17.00. Duties and Responsibilities Sanitation: All floors, surfaces, furniture, windows and windowsills, bathroom areas, and water fountains are cleaned daily. The standards of cleaning are developed by the Facilities Manager and regulated by current AAAHC standards. Housekeeping job responsibilities include the following: Ensure the following duties are accomplished between the hours of 4pm-10pm, Mon-Friday. Empty all trash in offices, provider’s areas, treatment rooms, and common spaces in the Thomson Building. Sweep and/or vacuum the elevator, all offices, provider spaces, treatment rooms, stairwells, and common spaces in the CHW and Thomson Building. Mop floors (if applicable), in the elevator, all offices, provider spaces, treatment rooms, stairwells, and common spaces in the CHW and Thomson Building. The following locations are considered high risk areas for germs, and should be wiped down, sterilized, and disinfected thoroughly each night: All Countertops, water fountains, door handles, elevator walls, hand sanitizers, stairwell railing, check in KIOSK , and common surfaces. Wipe down, sterilize, and disinfect desktops in offices. Do not move items on desktops or bookshelves. Work around these items. In restrooms, floors shall be swept and mopped, sinks sterilized/disinfected, toilet cleaned, sterilize/disinfected, walls and common surfaces sterilize/disinfected, and soap and towels should be replaced if needed. Turn off all lights, not located near a surveillance camera (lights to stay on are labeled). Lock all offices and provider areas after cleaning. Perform, special deep cleaning projects as assigned by the Evening Housekeeping Supervisor or the Facilities Manager Store cleaning supplies in designated storage areas in an orderly fashion. Enter time into time keeping database HR Peoplesoft no-later-than close of business every Friday. Attend monthly meeting with Evening Housekeeping Supervisor and the Facilities Manager. Qualifications One year of custodial, housekeeping or waste management experience is preferred. Must be able to perform moderately heavy physical duties (i.e. lifting waste cans, sweeping, mopping, vacuuming, etc.). Job Duties Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies Multiple vacancies Desired Start Date 05/05/2025 Proposed End Date 05/04/2026 Job Open Date 04/25/2025 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/186334 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in educational or employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender (including transgender), gender identity or expression, genetic information, HIV /AIDs status, military status, national origin, pregnancy (false pregnancy, termination of pregnancy, childbirth, recovery therefrom or related medical conditions, breastfeeding), race, religion (including religious dress and grooming practices), sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other bases under federal, state, local law, or regulations. Position Attributes Position Attributes Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. Safety/Security Sensitive or Requires a CDL No Hazardous weather category Essential Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Resume List of References and Contact Information To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
