    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/209913": {
      "title": "Custodian and Housekeeping Maintenance",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Custodian and Housekeeping Maintenance Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Custodian and Housekeeping Maintenance Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The application must be completed including all current and previous work history and education. A resume may be attached, but not substituted for completing work history and education sections of the application. USC Upstate offers a valuable benefits package including but not limited to: Health and Life Insurance Retirement Programs Paid Tuition Program Dependent Scholarships Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Annual Leave Sick Leave 13 Paid Holidays (including an extended December holiday) Paid Parental Leave Professional Development Opportunities Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number STA00550PO26 Job Family Building and Grounds Maintenance Job Function Custodial Services USC Market Title Custodial Lead Link to USC Market Title https://uscjobs.sc.edu/titles/132109 Job Level A3 - Administrative/Operational Support Business Title (Internal Title) Custodian and Housekeeping Maintenance Campus Upstate Work County Spartanburg College/Division USC Upstate College/Division Level Department UPS Facilities Grounds & Housekeeping State Pay Range G05 USC Market Range MRB - $36,608  $44,845  $53,082 Anticipated Hiring Range $36,608 - $43,994; Salary commensurate with education and experience. Location of Vacancy USC Upstate, Spartanburg, SC Part/Full Time Full Time Hours per Week 40 Work Schedule 2nd shift: Hours would be from 4:00 pm – 12:30 am, 40 hours per week. Must have the flexibility to work various shifts and/or weekends. Weekend Crew schedules would be scheduled on a rotational basis year-round. Must also have the ability to work overtime if required. Basis 12 months Job Search Category Trades/Maintenance About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Veterans' Preference Statement The University of South Carolina is committed to equal opportunity and proudly values the skills and experience military veterans bring to our workforce. Across South Carolina, we are making veterans a priority for employment and recognize their vital contributions to our state and our communities. Benefits for FTE Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers employees a valuable benefits package, including health and life insurance, generous paid leave and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Research Grant or Time-limited positions may be eligible for all, some, or no benefits, based on the grant or project funding. Position Description Advertised Job Summary Custodian and Housekeeping Maintenance University of South Carolina Upstate STA00550PO26 Spartanburg, SC The Custodian and Housekeeping Maintenance , under limited supervision from the Building Services Supervisor, performs various duties requiring skill and technical knowledge in general housekeeping, maintenance, and campus event set-up, flips, and break downs for all campus events. Works with Special Event Coordinator to ensure the location is fully equipped and prepared for smooth execution of events. Job Related Minimum Required Education and Experience Typically holds a high school diploma or GED . Requires 2 or more years of job related experience. Required Certification, Licensure/Other Credentials Valid driver’s license Successfully complete annual OSHA training. Preferred Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent and three years of related trade area and/or general maintenance experience. Proficiency with electronic work order systems and Microsoft Word and Excel Knowledge/Skills/Abilities A negative pre-employment drug screen is required. Subject to post-employment drug and alcohol testing per policy HR 1.95. A successful background check and good driving record is required. Ability to understand, carry out routine oral and written instructions as well as work independently and to direct work of others. Ability to recognize, acknowledge and troubleshoot solutions as they arise. Ability to receive and reliably execute oral and written instructions; communicate effectively verbally and in writing; prioritize and plan schedules; and establish and maintain effective working relationships with faculty, staff, students and the general public. Effective interpersonal and organizational skills. Must be a self-starter with knowledge in operational procedures, facility capabilities, event-related services and technical requirements for events in indoor and outdoor venues. Considerable knowledge and skill in use of tools, equipment and materials used in general building maintenance applicable to the job. Ability to make minor repairs and adjustments of equipment. Ability to work with computer and software systems for maintenance records. Exhibit large degree of flexibility with assignments. Must have knowledge of all campus buildings to be able to perform work in any building. Follow OSHA standards and guidelines when performing duties. Job Duties Job Duty Floor maintenance: Vacuum, shampoo carpets, dust mop, strip wax tile and hard surfaces floors. Furniture, sills, shelves: Dust and spot clean blackboards and erasers, realign classroom chairs, vacuum upholstered furniture. Doors, walls, ceilings and windows: clean glass, dust and spot clean, remove cobwebs. Fixtures: clean and sanitize toilets, urinals, sinks and drinking fountains, polish fixtures, clean mirrors. Containers: refill soap, towel and tissue dispensers. Waste containers: empty waste baskets and wipe clean. Be able to recognize and separate recyclable material from containers and take it to collection bins. Maintain equipment (vacuum, buffers, etc.). Serve as custodial floater for 2nd shift. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 40 Job Duty Remove and replace light bulbs, clean light fixtures of debris, perform minor electrical and plumbing repairs. As assigned through the SchoolDude work order system perform assigned repairs and maintenance as assigned which will include: general maintenance, painting, carpentry, basic plumbing and electrical that does not require certification. Under hazardous weather conditions will perform snow and ice removal. Must be able to handle minor emergency repairs in each of these areas. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 40 Job Duty Provide assistance set up for special events. Event set-ups/flips/breakdowns: Set up required resources (tables, chairs, stages, podiums, flooring, stanchions, etc.) for each venue event as requested by customer. All set-ups will be neat, clean, orderly and in good working condition. Venues will be set up and broken down as outlined in work order and instructed by Facilities Special Event Coordinator. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 15 Job Duty Other duties as assigned. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 5 Position Attributes Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. Safety Sensitive or Security Sensitive Yes Hazardous weather category Essential Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 08/03/2026 Job Open Date 07/20/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant The application must be completed including all current and previous work history and education. A resume may be attached, but not substituted for completing work history and education sections of the application. USC Upstate offers a valuable benefits package including but not limited to: Health and Life Insurance Retirement Programs Paid Tuition Program Dependent Scholarships Employee Assistance Program ( EAP ) Annual Leave Sick Leave 13 Paid Holidays (including an extended December holiday) Paid Parental Leave Professional Development Opportunities Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/209903 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in educational or employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender (including transgender), gender identity or expression, genetic information, HIV /AIDs status, military status, national origin, pregnancy (false pregnancy, termination of pregnancy, childbirth, recovery therefrom or related medical conditions, breastfeeding), race, religion (including religious dress and grooming practices), sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other bases under federal, state, local law, or regulations. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This University of South Carolina Upstate position is located in Spartanburg, South Carolina. \r\n\r\nDo you wish to continue applying for this position? Yes No * Are you willing and able to submit to a pre-employment background check that may include, but it is not limited to, criminal history, national sex offender search and motor vehicle history as a condition of hire? Yes No * Do you have a high school diploma or equivalent and three years of related trade area and/or general maintenance experience? Yes No * List any certification or training related to custodial and maintenance operations. (Open Ended Question) * What does SDS stand for and what is the purpose of the SDS sheet? (Open Ended Question) * Are you familiar with any aspects of OSHA? If so, please describe any relevant training or experience. (Open Ended Question) * Describe any experience you have regarding floor work in detail. Additionally, list any equipment you have used for floor work (Open Ended Question) * Describe any experience you have regarding carpet cleaning methods in detail. Additionally, list any equipment you have used for carpet cleaning. (Open Ended Question) * Regarding Blood Borne Pathogens, please explain in detail the steps you would take for any clean-up procedures while including any safety measures, the appropriate PPE and why. (Open Ended Question) * Describe any experience, training, or certification you have regarding the use of disinfection protocols? (Open Ended Question) * Describe any experience, training, or certification you have regarding light mechanical maintenance? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a valid driver's license and good driving record? Yes No * Are you willing to pass a pre-employment alcohol and drug test consistent with USC HR Policy 1.95, Drug and Alcohol Testing? Yes No * The salary range for this position is $36,608 - $43,994 based on education and experience. Is this salary range acceptable to you? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Supporting Documents Resume List of References and Contact Information To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
