    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/212245": {
      "title": "Housing Maintenance",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Housing Maintenance Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Housing Maintenance Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Positions will remain posted on our employment website for a minimum of five (5) business days. After this period, postings may be closed at the department’s discretion. Our site is updated regularly, and the length of the recruitment and screening process may vary depending on the position and related factors. If your qualifications are selected for further consideration, you will be contacted directly by phone or email. The University of South Carolina offers a valuable benefits package including but not limited to: Health and Life Insurance Retirement Programs Paid Tuition Dependent Scholarships Annual Leave Sick Leave 13 Paid Holidays (including an extended December holiday) Paid Parental Leave Professional Development Opportunities Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number STA00594PO26 Job Family Building and Grounds Maintenance Job Function Facilities Maintenance USC Market Title Maintenance Tech Link to USC Market Title https://uscjobs.sc.edu/titles/132148 Job Level T1 - Technical Support Business Title (Internal Title) Housing Maintenance Campus Beaufort Work County Beaufort College/Division USC Beaufort College/Division Level Department BFT Maintenance Services State Pay Range G05 USC Market Range MRB - $36,608  $44,845  $53,082 Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with experience and education Location of Vacancy USC Beaufort supported area Part/Full Time Full Time Hours per Week 40 Work Schedule Standard working schedule: Monday – Friday 8:30am – 5:00pm, with one hour for lunch, Must be willing to work a flexible schedule to meet the needs of the department. Can include nights and weekends. Basis 12 months Job Search Category Other Professional About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Veterans' Preference Statement The University of South Carolina is committed to equal opportunity and proudly values the skills and experience military veterans bring to our workforce. Across South Carolina, we are making veterans a priority for employment and recognize their vital contributions to our state and our communities. Benefits for FTE Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers employees a valuable benefits package, including health and life insurance, generous paid leave and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Research Grant or Time-limited positions may be eligible for all, some, or no benefits, based on the grant or project funding. Position Description Advertised Job Summary Housing Maintenance Technician University of South Carolina Beaufort ( USCB ) – Beaufort & Bluffton, South Carolina Help Create Exceptional Student Living Experiences on the South Carolina Coast! The University of South Carolina Beaufort ( USCB ) is seeking a motivated, dependable, and skilled Housing Maintenance Technician to join our Facilities team. Located in the heart of South Carolina’s beautiful Lowcountry, with campuses near Hilton Head Island, Savannah, and Charleston, USCB offers a unique opportunity to build your career while making a direct impact on the student experience. If you enjoy solving problems, working with your hands, and taking pride in maintaining safe, attractive, and welcoming residential communities, we invite you to become part of our growing university. What You’ll Do As a Housing Maintenance Technician, you will play a vital role in ensuring our residence halls remain safe, functional, and comfortable for students by: Performing preventive maintenance and repairs throughout university housing facilities. Troubleshooting and repairing residential appliances, including washers, dryers, refrigerators, ovens, and other kitchen equipment. Performing plumbing repairs, including toilets, sinks, shower ﬁxtures, faucets, and drains. Completing general maintenance work in carpentry, electrical, plumbing, masonry, painting, and minor renovations. Responding promptly to maintenance requests through the university’s computerized work order system. Assisting with room renovations, installations, and facility improvement projects. Inspecting housing facilities to identify maintenance concerns before they become larger issues. Maintaining tools, equipment, and supplies needed to perform daily responsibilities safely and eﬃciently. Working independently or as part of a collaborative facilities team to deliver exceptional service to students and campus partners. Helping maintain the overall appearance, safety, and operational readiness of university housing facilities and surrounding grounds. What We’re Looking For The ideal candidate is someone who: Has experience in building maintenance, facilities management, or one or more skilled trades. Possesses working knowledge of plumbing, electrical, carpentry, appliance repair, and general maintenance. Enjoys troubleshooting problems and ﬁnding practical solutions. Takes pride in providing excellent customer service to students, faculty, and staff. Works effectively both independently and as part of a team. Demonstrates strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Is committed to maintaining a safe, clean, and welcoming campus environment. Why Join USCB ? At the University of South Carolina Beaufort, every employee contributes to creating an outstanding student experience. As a Housing Maintenance Technician, you’ll enjoy meaningful work while living and working in one of the nation’s most desirable coastal regions. From historic Beaufort to the beaches of Hilton Head Island and the vibrant culture of nearby Savannah and Charleston, the Lowcountry offers an unmatched quality of life. Be Part of Something Bigger Your skills help create the home away from home where students learn, grow, and thrive. Join a university committed to excellence, innovation, and student success while enjoying an exceptional career in South Carolina’s beautiful coastal Lowcountry. Please be prepared to upload a current resume and references w/ contact information. Apply today and help build the future—one residence hall at a time—at the University of South Carolina Beaufort! Job Related Minimum Required Education and Experience Requires accreditation from a technical school or an applicable skilled trades program and no prior work experience, which may be substituted by an equivalent combination of job related certification, training, education, and/or experience. Required Certification, Licensure/Other Credentials Preferred Qualifications Knowledge/Skills/Abilities Knowledge of safety practices, tools, equipment, materials and supplies used in maintenance of buildings. Skills in making emergency and general repairs and adjustments to equipment used in building and maintenance work. Ability to perform heavy manual labor. Job Duties Job Duty Performs maintenance and repair tasks in such areas as carpentry, masonry, electrical, and plumbing. Maintains equipment used in all parts of job. Works through work order system to complete orders as assigned. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 40 Job Duty Trouble shoot and performs minor repairs on appliances, such as washer/dryer, kitchen appliances. Replaces as necessary. Repairs plumbing as needed. Includes toilets, shower heads and kitchen fixtures. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 20 Job Duty Performs routine cleaning of breezeways and entrances, including removing debris of exterior hallways, entrances and stairways. Blow leaves from areas. Report and damages to supervisor. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 20 Job Duty Performs minor repairs to exterior finishes and interior walls, floors as needed. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 10 Job Duty Responds to emergency repairs to provide protection of building and safety of students. Contacts appropriate Facilities and Housing staff to report emergency repairs. Secures facility until further assessment can be made to determine extent of repairs needed. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 10 Position Attributes Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. Safety Sensitive or Security Sensitive No Hazardous weather category Non-Essential Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date Job Open Date 08/05/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant Positions will remain posted on our employment website for a minimum of five (5) business days. After this period, postings may be closed at the department’s discretion. Our site is updated regularly, and the length of the recruitment and screening process may vary depending on the position and related factors. If your qualifications are selected for further consideration, you will be contacted directly by phone or email. The University of South Carolina offers a valuable benefits package including but not limited to: Health and Life Insurance Retirement Programs Paid Tuition Dependent Scholarships Annual Leave Sick Leave 13 Paid Holidays (including an extended December holiday) Paid Parental Leave Professional Development Opportunities Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/211098 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an accreditation from a technical school or an applicable skilled trades program? Yes No * Do you have knowledge of safety practices? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume List of References and Contact Information Optional Documents Other Supporting Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
