    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/211208": {
      "title": "Position Attributes",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Access Service Temp Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Access Service Temp Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number TMP01938PO26 Job Code Title Library Specialist Advertised Title Access Service Temp Campus Columbia College/Division University Libraries Department LIBR Access Services Salary 18.00 hr. Location of Vacancy Part/Full Time Part Time Hours per Week 25 Work Schedule Monday – Friday 1pm-6pm Job Search Category Other Professional About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Benefits for Temporary Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers temporary employees expected to work at least 30 hours per week health and life insurance, flexible spending accounts and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary The Temporary Library Specialist provides support for the daily operations of the Access Services Department by performing a variety of customer service and circulation-related functions. This position assists with circulation, interlibrary loan ( ILL ), document delivery, and course reserves to ensure efficient access to library collections and services for students, faculty, staff, and community users. The position requires excellent customer service, attention to detail, and the ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provide courteous and professional customer service at the Access Services desk, in person, by phone, and through email. Perform circulation functions including checking materials in and out, processing renewals, collecting fines and fees as applicable, and assisting patrons with library accounts. Process, receive, and fulfill interlibrary loan ( ILL ) borrowing and lending requests using established library systems and procedures. Manage document delivery requests by retrieving, scanning, and electronically delivering library materials in accordance with copyright guidelines and library policies. Assist with the preparation, processing, maintenance, and removal of course reserve materials, including print and electronic reserves. Retrieve, shelve, shift, and maintain library collections to ensure accurate organization and accessibility. Process returned materials and identify items requiring repair, replacement, or special handling. Follow established library policies, procedures, and confidentiality standards. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent; bachelor’s degree preferred. Customer service experience in a library, educational, or public service environment preferred. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Ability to learn and use integrated library systems, interlibrary loan software, and standard office applications. Ability to prioritize multiple tasks while maintaining accuracy. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in an academic library. Familiarity with integrated library systems (such as Alma, Sierra, Koha, or similar). Experience using interlibrary loan platforms such as ILLiad, Tipasa, or OCLC resource sharing systems. Knowledge of copyright and fair use as they relate to document delivery and course reserves. Physical Requirements Ability to stand, walk, bend, and reach for extended periods. Ability to lift and move library materials weighing up to 25 pounds. Ability to push and pull book carts throughout the library. Job Duties Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 08/17/2026 Proposed End Date 12/18/2026 Job Open Date 08/07/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/211178 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in educational or employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender (including transgender), gender identity or expression, genetic information, HIV /AIDs status, military status, national origin, pregnancy (false pregnancy, termination of pregnancy, childbirth, recovery therefrom or related medical conditions, breastfeeding), race, religion (including religious dress and grooming practices), sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other bases under federal, state, local law, or regulations. Position Attributes Position Attributes Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. Safety/Security Sensitive or Requires a CDL No Hazardous weather category Non-Essential Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a high school diploma or equivalent? Yes No * Do you have a bachelor's degree? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents List of References and Contact Information Optional Documents Other Supporting Documents Resume To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/161449": {
      "title": "Position Attributes",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Adjunct Faculty in History Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Adjunct Faculty in History Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. An unofficial transcript must be attached in addition to the required application, cover letter, and vitae. If you are unable to attach an electronic version of your official transcript you may mail a copy to the Office of Human Resources, USC Sumter, 200 Miller Road, Sumter, SC 29150. If you have any questions about the application procedures, please call (803)938-3721. If you are hired to teach for USC Sumter, you will be required to submit an official copy of your transcripts. Review of credentials will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. USC Sumter is an Affirmative Action and Equal Opportunity Employer. Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number TMP03014PO21 Job Code Title Lecturer Advertised Title Adjunct Faculty in History Campus Sumter College/Division USC Sumter College/Division Level Department USC Sumter - Palmetto College Salary Salary commensurate with education & experience Location of Vacancy Richland, Lexington and Sumter counties Part/Full Time Part Time Hours per Week 20 Work Schedule Job Search Category Faculty About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Benefits for Temporary Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers temporary employees expected to work at least 30 hours per week health and life insurance, flexible spending accounts and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary USC Sumter is seeking an Adjunct Instructor in History to teach HIST 101 and 102: European Civilization and/or HIST 111 and 112: History of the United States. Courses may be in-person in Lexington, Richland, or Sumter Counties, or online. Candidates should possess a Master’s degree and a minimum of 18 graduate hours in the discipline. Master’s Degree or Ph.D. in the discipline preferred. Please indicate your interest in teaching in person and/or online. Teaching experience in post-secondary education and with online instruction is desired. Experience teaching the above-named course(s) or equivalent is ideal. This appointment is on a course-by-course basis. Salary is commensurate with education, experience and discipline. Qualifications Candidates must have either a completed Ph.D. or be currently pursuing a Ph.D. with at least 18 graduate hours in History and specific coursework in the field being taught. Job Duties Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies Multiple Desired Start Date 01/10/2022 Proposed End Date Job Open Date 11/16/2021 Job Close Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant An unofficial transcript must be attached in addition to the required application, cover letter, and vitae. If you are unable to attach an electronic version of your official transcript you may mail a copy to the Office of Human Resources, USC Sumter, 200 Miller Road, Sumter, SC 29150. If you have any questions about the application procedures, please call (803)938-3721. If you are hired to teach for USC Sumter, you will be required to submit an official copy of your transcripts. Review of credentials will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. USC Sumter is an Affirmative Action and Equal Opportunity Employer. Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/109912 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in educational or employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender (including transgender), gender identity or expression, genetic information, HIV /AIDs status, military status, national origin, pregnancy (false pregnancy, termination of pregnancy, childbirth, recovery therefrom or related medical conditions, breastfeeding), race, religion (including religious dress and grooming practices), sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other bases under federal, state, local law, or regulations. Position Attributes Position Attributes Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. Safety/Security Sensitive or Requires a CDL No Hazardous weather category Non-Essential Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Other Supporting Documents List of References and Contact Information Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
