les. Knowledge of customer service, accounting, bookkeeping and handling of cash. Understanding of library services for people with disabilities. Ability to manage a library department. Ability to analyze requests and select best reference sources. Ability to perform detailed work with accuracy. Ability to communicate effectively. Ability to work independently and exercise initiative. Ability to perform instruction and/or provide informational workshops to students about library services. Job Duties Job Duty Library Services: Circulation, reference, research, cataloging, acquisitions, collection development, interlibrary loan, PASCAL , media, library instruction. Reviewing policies and procedures, observations, analysis, assessment, reports and suggestions for strategic goals. Work with Head Librarian and Associate Dean to suggest and implement strategic goals for increase growth in library spaces. Plan and coordinate engagement activities promoting the library. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 60 Job Duty Instruction, professional development and service to the profession and campus by conducting informational workshops to the community and students about library services, participate in campus committees, and participate in professional development opportunities available through the university and outside sources to ensure the library stays current and relevant. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 25 Job Duty Supervisory: Hire, train, supervise and evaluate temporary staff, work-study/institutional student workers. Provide adequate staffing and assure library is open on time and during designated hours. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 10 Job Duty Assist with special projects, events and other routine support activities as required. Attend committee meetings. Other duties as assigned. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 5 Position Attributes Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. Safety Sensitive or Security Sensitive No Hazardous weather category Non-Essential Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 09/01/2026 Job Open Date 08/10/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Please provide complete contact information for references including phone numbers and email addresses. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/211354 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume List of References and Contact Information Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
