    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/159657": {
      "title": "Group Fitness Instructor",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Group Fitness Instructor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Group Fitness Instructor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number STU00052PO23 Job Title Student Employee Internal Title Group Fitness Instructor Campus Upstate College/Division USC Upstate College/Division Level Department UPS Campus Recreation Advertised Salary $12 - $14 per hour depending on certifications Location of Vacancy USC Upstate, Spartanburg, SC Part/Full Time Part Time Hours per week 10 Work Schedule Up to 10 hours per week. Weekly scheduled to be determined and will vary, but student employee must be able to work flexible hours to include some evenings and weekends Job Search Category Student Employee Position Description Advertised Job Summary - Develop and lead fitness classes. Student instructors must feel comfortable in front of a group and be able to teach proper form and alignment for movements and exercises dynamically. Duties and Responsibilities - Develop and lead safe and effective group fitness classes, providing modifications to accommodate all participants - Vary routines, music, and classes while following established/recognized protocol of the Wellness Center, AFAA , etc. - Prepare and use appropriate music and equipment - Educate participants on proper form, anatomy, and modification of moves - Provide individual feedback to participants throughout the class - Ensure that safety standards are met and appropriate policies and procedures are followed - Responsible for appropriate use of all Group Fitness related equipment - Teach scheduled classes that begin and end on time - Arrive early to prepare and set up all equipment and stay after class to put away equipment, lock up stereo closet, and be available to participants - Inspect the aerobics rooms and all equipment to ensure they are clean and safe for patron use - Report and restrict use of broken equipment - Greet each participant in a welcoming manner - Inspire each participant to reach his/her fitness goals - Promote and role model positive self-image and lifestyle habits to your participants - Responsible for own class coverage when unavailable to attend - Monitor and record attendance of participants - Uphold Campus Recreation’s mission - Attend and actively participate in all mandatory staff meetings and training sessions - Thoroughly complete all incident reports, report all injuries, vandalism, equipment needs, and problems immediately to administrative staff - Maintain regular communication with the Assistant Director – Fitness and/or student supervisor - Handle any other duties as assigned by the Assistant Director – Fitness and/or student supervisor Expectations: - Ability to develop and instruct 30-60 minute group fitness classes for students, faculty, and staff on a regular basis - Ability to provide own music and programs and be comfortable leading a class - Maintain current group exercise instructor certification(s) including obtaining CECs/CEUs as required - Maintain a minimum class attendance - Present self in approachable, friendly manner with a willingness to help a diverse range of users Qualifications Preferred Qualifications - Nationally recognized group exercise instructor certification ( ACE or AFAA ) or specialty certification as needed - Experience working with diverse populations - Strong interpersonal, communication, and leadership skills - Physical Education/Exercise Science major - Additional training in specialty formats may be required A strong preference will be given to applicants who submit a one-page cover letter describing their interest in the open position and any related experience. Respond to the following supplemental statements. 1.) List name of certifications held and dates of expiration. A copy of your certification will be required before hire. 2.) List type of class(es) you are qualified to teach and preferred number of classes per week. 3.) List any/all previous teaching experience (if applicable). Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 2-5 Desired Start Date 01/08/2024 Job Open Date 12/01/2023 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/159655 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in educational or employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender (including transgender), gender identity or expression, genetic information, HIV /AIDs status, military status, national origin, pregnancy (false pregnancy, termination of pregnancy, childbirth, recovery therefrom or related medical conditions, breastfeeding), race, religion (including religious dress and grooming practices), sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other bases under federal, state, local law, or regulations. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your expected graduation date? (Open Ended Question) * What is your current cumulative GPA? (Open Ended Question) * Have you worked on-campus before? (Open Ended Question) * If yes, list department name and supervisor. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently working another on-campus job? (Open Ended Question) * If yes, list department name and supervisor. (Open Ended Question) * Have you been awarded Federal Work Study for this semester? Yes No * What is your major? (Open Ended Question) * What is your current student status? Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate Student * What is your College affiliation? Please list one of the following: Business Administration & Economics College of Arts & Sciences Department of Psychology Education Fine Arts & Communication Studies Interdisciplinary Studies Information Management Systems Language, Literature & Composition Math & Computer Science Natural Sciences Non-Profit Administration Nursing Pre-Professional Social & Behavioral Sciences Social Sciences, Philosophy & History Undeclared (Open Ended Question) * Why are you interested in this position? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a current National Fitness Certification (i.e.: ACE, AFAA, NETA, ACSM, etc.)? If selected for interview, be prepared to show proof. Yes No * If yes, when does your National Fitness Certification expire? If selected for an interview, be prepared to show proof. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter Resume List of References and Contact Information To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
