      "title": "Position Attributes",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Electrician Helper Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Electrician Helper Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Fill out application with all experience. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number TMP02282PO26 Job Code Title Trades Specialist III Advertised Title Electrician Helper Campus Columbia College/Division Division of Student Affairs and Academic Support Department SAAS Custodial, Move Crew and Facilities Administration Salary 19.62/per hour Location of Vacancy Part/Full Time Full Time Hours per Week 40 Work Schedule Standard working schedule: 8:00am – 4:30pm Monday – Friday Must be willing to work a flexible schedule to meet the needs of the department. Job Search Category Trades/Maintenance About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Benefits for Temporary Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers temporary employees expected to work at least 30 hours per week health and life insurance, flexible spending accounts and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary Electrician Helper Do you enjoy not sitting behind a desk? Do you enjoy helping USC Students? Do you enjoy troubleshooting challenges by finding solutions, especially unique challenges? Would you like to build foundational trade skills in a supportive and educational university environment? This is the job for you. The Electrician Helper, will assist the Electrical Technician across a variety of functions essential to the maintenance/repair/troubleshooting of electrical systems/components. This entry-level position offers a hands-on learning experience for individuals interested in developing skills in the trades. Essential Job Duties and Responsibilities: Assists paired technician with installation, troubleshooting, programming, repairs and modifications on a variety of electrical equipment. Performs basic tasks while operating tools and machinery under direct supervision of paired technician or designee. Sets up necessary staging areas, lay down protective coverings, and ensure all tools and materials are brought to the work area. Maintains a clean, organized, and safe job site during and after completion. Transports materials and supplies. Performs basic inspections and reporting issues to the appropriate personnel while strictly following all safety protocols. Submits work orders when appropriate. This position is designated as essential personnel during inclement/hazardous weather and other emergencies. Potential for Full Time Employee ( FTE ) position based on job performance. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency and related trade experience. Valid Driver’s License required. Job Duties Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies Multiple Desired Start Date 10/01/2026 Proposed End Date 12/18/2026 Job Open Date 09/04/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Fill out application with all experience. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/212905 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Position Attributes Position Attributes Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. Safety/Security Sensitive or Requires a CDL No Hazardous weather category Essential Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have at least a high school diploma or equivalency and related trade experience? Yes No * Do you have a Valid Driver's License? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents List of References and Contact Information Optional Documents Resume To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
