    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/169196": {
      "title": "Position Attributes",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Technology Commercialization Consultant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Technology Commercialization Consultant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position will be located in North Charleston, SC. T his position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number TMP01082PO24 Job Code Title Program Manager I Advertised Title Technology Commercialization Consultant Campus Columbia College/Division Darla Moore School of Business Department DMSB Small Business Development Center Salary $30 - $35/hourly Location of Vacancy Part/Full Time Part Time Hours per Week 24 Work Schedule Standard working schedule: 9:00am – 5:00pm Monday through Friday work week. Specifics of hours and days to be determined. Must be willing to work a flexible schedule to meet the needs of the department. Normal business hours and may include some evening or weekend hours for special events. Job Search Category Other Professional About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Benefits for Temporary Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers temporary employees expected to work at least 30 hours per week health and life insurance, flexible spending accounts and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary The Technology Commercialization Consultant facilitates the growth of small, high-tech, innovative, and fast-growing companies in South Carolina. Primary duties are: 1. Provide private consulting to small businesses and entrepreneurs on the viability of new technology/product concepts, business planning, IP research/protection, identifying and helping to secure funding support through SBIR / STTR and other government contracts, providing guidance on contract performance, etc. 2. Conduct educational seminars and workshops on technology commercialization in the assigned territory. 3. Develop network/partnerships to expand assistance and connect clients with other resources. This work will be provided in conjunction with general management services offered by core Small Business Development Centers ( SBDC ) and Procurement Technical Assistance Program ( PTAP ) advisors, including team or co-consulting. Qualifications Minimum qualifications: Master’s degree in related field and 2 years relevant program experience, or bachelor’s degree and 4 years relevant program experience. Preferred Qualifications: Small business and technology commercialization experience. Strong communication skills. Grant writing and consulting experience. Job Duties Job Duty Maintain documentation as required by the SC SBDC and its funding sources including entering all client activity and results into the database.  Stay abreast of full SC SBDC network programs and priorities in order to integrate the tech commercialization effort into the organization’s operation.  Work with the State Director and other Tech Consultants to further develop this initiative and gain national technology commercialization accreditation.  Participate in selection of other tech positions. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 10 Job Duty Develop and conduct seminars (alone or with partners) for groups of small business clients/entrepreneurs that build understanding of government grants/contracts, how to incorporate new products into the company’s strategic plan and other topics on successful commercialization. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 20 Job Duty Develop strategic partnerships and collaborations that expand on SC SBDC services to further promote the growth and success of S.C. technology based companies.  Stay abreast of federal, state and regional economic development initiatives and support programs in order to help clients capitalize on these opportunities.  Provide connections between clients and university faculty/potential customers/strategic partners in order to help them execute strategic alliances, partnerships, licensing agreements, etc.  Initiate and help coordinate projects to match students with SBDC clients as appropriate. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 20 Job Duty Provide business consulting assistance in areas including commercialization and growth strategies, financing, IP strategy, business management and networking.  A significant part of this role is providing guidance on identifying SBIR / STTR and other grant/contract opportunities, assisting with review and submissions and providing ongoing coaching/mentoring after award.  Help clients achieve goals and create measurable economic impact as defined by the SBDC . Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 50 Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 07/01/2024 Proposed End Date 12/16/2024 Job Open Date 06/01/2024 Job Close Date 12/16/2024 Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant This position will be located in North Charleston, SC. T his position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/168351 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in educational or employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender (including transgender), gender identity or expression, genetic information, HIV /AIDs status, military status, national origin, pregnancy (false pregnancy, termination of pregnancy, childbirth, recovery therefrom or related medical conditions, breastfeeding), race, religion (including religious dress and grooming practices), sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other bases under federal, state, local law, or regulations. Position Attributes Position Attributes Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. Safety/Security Sensitive or Requires a CDL No Hazardous weather category Non-Essential Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume List of References and Contact Information Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 Curriculum Vitae To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
