    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/201903": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Clinical Instructor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Clinical Instructor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Posting Details To navigate through this form, please use the “Prev” and “Save & Continue” buttons at the top of the page. Do not use your browser’s “Back” button as it will not save your progress and data will be lost. Posting Summary Logo Posting Number RTF00126PO24 USC Market Title Clinical Instructor Link to USC Market Title https://uscjobs.sc.edu/titles/8202/ Business Title Clinical Instructor Campus Columbia Work County Richland College/Division College of Pharmacy Department COP Clinical Pharmacy and Outcomes Sciences Location of Vacancy Part/Full Time Full Time Hours per Week 37.5 Type of Faculty Position Faculty Time-Limited (FTL) Basis 12 months Job Search Category Other Professional About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Benefits for Research Grant or Time-Limited Positions Are Indicated Below The University of South Carolina (UofSC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers employees a valuable benefits package, including health and life insurance, generous paid leave and retirement programs. To learn more about UofSC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Research Grant or Time-limited positions may be eligible for all, some, or no benefits, based on the grant or project funding. South Carolina Retirement Yes State Insurance Programs Yes Annual Leave Yes Sick Leave Yes Position Description Advertised Job Summary The University of South Carolina College of Pharmacy is recruiting for a pharmacy resident position of 1-year duration. The resident pharmacist will be hired as a Clinical Instructor in the COP . The resident is expected to perform applicable duties associated with a clinical partner Tandem Health. The duties include conducting patient care duties fulfilled through rotational experiences as outlined by residency leadership and the affiliated clinical partner. To conduct quality initiatives and a major research project as approved by residency leadership adhere to American Society of Health-System Pharmacists residency standards related to practice, research, and professionalism. To attend required conferences, meetings, and professional development opportunities outlined by residency leadership. To Complete the Clinical Teaching Certificate program through the College of Pharmacy. This position is from July 1, 2024 – June 30th 2025. Job Related Minimum Required Education and Experience Doctor of Pharmacy degree from ACPE -accredited College/School of Pharmacy PGY1 and PGY2For PGY2 positions only, completion of an ASHP -accredited PGY1 programAvailable for pharmacist licensure in the state of South Carolina Required Certification, Licensure/Other Credentials Preferred Qualifications Doctor of Pharmacy degree from ACPE -accredited College/School of Pharmacy PGY1 and PGY2 For PGY2 positions only, completion of an ASHP -accredited PGY1 program. Available for pharmacist licensure in the state of South Carolina Knowledge/Skills/Abilities Excellent written and oral communication teaching skills, adequate clinical competence, professional ethics, and sufficient clinical experience. Completion of a PGY1 residency from an ASHP -accredited program. Job Duties Job Duty To conduct patient care through rotational experiences outlined by residency requirements and by affiliated clinical partners. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 50 Job Duty To conduct quality initiatives and conduct a major research project approved by the Residency leadership and also work on Rural health projects. Will work with statewide stewardship initiatives across the continuum of care. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 30 Job Duty To provide service to the college and profession through pharmacy organizations (e.g. local, state/regional, and/or national). To attend required conferences, meetings, and professional development opportunities outlined by residency leadership. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 10 Job Duty To complete the Clinical Teaching Certificate Program provided by College of Pharmacy Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 10 Position Attributes Hazardous weather category Non-Essential Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. No Posting Detail Information Desired Start Date 07/01/2024 Position End Date 06/30/2025 Job Open Date 04/23/2024 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/167310 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in educational or employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender (including transgender), gender identity or expression, genetic information, HIV /AIDs status, military status, national origin, pregnancy (false pregnancy, termination of pregnancy, childbirth, recovery therefrom or related medical conditions, breastfeeding), race, religion (including religious dress and grooming practices), sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other bases under federal, state, local law, or regulations. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References and Contact Information Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
