      "title": "Poison Center",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Poison Center - Nurse Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Poison Center - Nurse Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. We are only accepting applications submitted by September 16, 2026. Posting Details To navigate through this form, please use the “Prev” and “Save & Continue” buttons at the top of the page. Do not use your browser’s “Back” button as it will not save your progress and data will be lost. Posting Summary Logo Posting Number RTF00190PO26 USC Market Title Registered Nurse Link to USC Market Title https://uscjobs.sc.edu/titles/156299 Business Title (Internal Title) Poison Center - Nurse Campus Columbia Work County Richland College/Division College of Pharmacy Department COP South Carolina Poison Center Anticipated Hiring Range $69,913-$104,870 Location of Vacancy Columbia, SC Part/Full Time Full Time Hours per Week 37.5 Work Schedule Standard working schedule: 8:30am – 5:00pm Must be willing to work a flexible schedule to meet the needs of the department. Type of Staff Position Staff Research Grant (SRGP) Basis 12 months Job Search Category Other About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Benefits for Research Grant or Time-Limited Positions Are Indicated Below The University of South Carolina (UofSC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers employees a valuable benefits package, including health and life insurance, generous paid leave and retirement programs. To learn more about UofSC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Research Grant or Time-limited positions may be eligible for all, some, or no benefits, based on the grant or project funding. South Carolina Retirement Yes State Insurance Programs Yes Annual Leave Yes Sick Leave Yes Position Description Advertised Job Summary The Poison Center Nurse for the South Carolina Poison Center provides professional nursing assessment, triage, consultation, and follow-up services to healthcare professionals and the public regarding poison exposures and drug information. Under general supervision, this position applies established toxicology protocols and nursing judgment to assess exposure risk, provide care recommendations, and support appropriate patient outcomes. The primary goal of the position is to deliver accurate, timely, and evidence-based poison management guidance that supports patient safety and public health. Job Related Minimum Required Education and Experience Requires a bachelor’s degree in a job related field and 3 or more years of job related experience, which may be substituted by an equivalent combination of job related certification, training, education, and/or experience. Required Certification, Licensure/Other Credentials Licensure as a registered nurse by the South Carolina Board of Nursing. Preferred Qualifications Recent emergency room or critical care experience. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities Strong interpersonal and communication skills. The ability to communicate medical information to health care professionals and to the public over the telephone under crisis circumstances is essential. Knowledge of basic data entry and documentation necessary. Capable of making immediate and accurate professional decisions in providing information and consultations. Job Duties Job Duty Provide Poison Exposure Assessment and Consultation Respond to poison exposure and drug information inquiries from healthcare professionals and the public to promote safe and appropriate patient care. Utilize established clinical protocols, toxicology resources, and nursing judgment to assess exposure severity, recommend treatment or referral, and determine need for follow-up. Conduct follow-up calls as appropriate to monitor patient progress and outcomes. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 50 Job Duty Maintain Accurate Clinical Documentation Document consultations, assessments, recommendations, and follow-up activities in the poison center electronic data management system to ensure accurate records, regulatory compliance, and continuity of care. Review entries for completeness and accuracy in accordance with quality standards. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 20 Job Duty Support Clinical Operations and Training Assist in orienting and guiding student assistants and poison information providers in the use of protocols and documentation procedures to ensure consistent service delivery and adherence to center standards. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 10 Job Duty Participate in Quality Assurance and Research Activities Participate in case review, data collection, and quality improvement initiatives to support ongoing evaluation and enhancement of poison center services. Assist with research or scholarly activities as assigned. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 10 Job Duty Maintain Professional Competency Maintain current nursing licensure and required continuing education. Stay informed of developments in toxicology and emergency care to ensure provision of current and reliable information. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 10 Position Attributes Hazardous weather category Essential Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. No Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date Position End Date Job Open Date 08/18/2026 Job Close Date 09/16/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. We are only accepting applications submitted by September 16, 2026. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/211821 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have at least a Bachelor’s Degree in a job related field and 3 or more years of job related experience, which may be substituted by an equivalent combination of job related certification, training, education, and/or experience? Yes No * Are you licensed as a registered nurse by the South Carolina Board of Nursing? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume List of References and Contact Information Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
